   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n<p><span>Dear all,</span></p><p><span>For R users interested in exploring how AI tools can support their everyday workflows, we are offering a hands-on online workshop: </span><strong><span>“Integrating Large Language Model Tools into R Workflows”</span></strong><span> on </span><strong><span>4 August</span></strong><span>.</span></p><p><span><br></span></p><p><span>Course website: </span><a href=\"https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/llms-4-r-fsbi/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/llms-4-r-fsbi/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792412521755000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3u1jnedEfji0a14iwEhVKp\">https://www.physalia-courses.org/courses-workshops/llms-4-r-fsbi/</a> </p><p><span>The workshop will cover practical ways to use LLMs for:</span><br><span>• generating, editing, documenting, and troubleshooting R code</span><br><span>• assisting with data cleaning and visualization</span><br><span>• integrating AI tools into RStudio and Positron workflows</span><br><span>• working with model APIs directly from R</span><br><span>• exploring advanced use cases such as structured data extraction from PDFs</span></p><p><span>The focus is on practical, responsible, and reproducible use of LLMs in research workflows. No prior LLM experience is needed—basic R experience is enough.</span></p><p><span><br></span></p><p><span>Best regards,</span></p><p><span>Carlo</span></p><p><span><br></span></p><p>\r\n--------------------<br><br>Carlo Pecoraro, Ph.D<br><br><br>Physalia-courses DIRECTOR<br><br><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">in...@physalia-courses.org</a>\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
